{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are sequences of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" symbols, stored as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"text":" holds words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"text":" the same words scalar by scalar, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"text":" byte strings. Lookup,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for a key of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and at most ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/PrefixView"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/count","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/isEmpty"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/contains(_:)-6tnqd","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/